			<abstract label="Abstract:" encodinganalog="520$a">Minutes, reports, correspondence and other material created or collected by the Office of Student Life and Diversity, including records related to the ALANA Center and various student groups. Also included are audiovisual materials, including VHS and compact disc recordings of baccalaureate ceremonies; photographs; event flyers and posters; and realia including mugs, t-shirts, and pens.</abstract>
		</did>
		<bioghist encodinganalog="545">
			<head>Administrative History</head>
			<p>The history of the Campus Life and Diversity Office is closely tied to the Vassar career of Edward Pittman. Pittman, a member of Vassar's Class of 1982, began working for the college in 1990 in the newly-created Office of Multicultural Affairs, a division of the Dean of Student Life.</p>
		</bioghist>
		<bioghist encodinganalog="545">
			<head>Chronology</head>
			<chronlist>
				<chronitem>
					<date>1974 September</date>
					<event>President Alan Simpson appointed Serge Paul-Emile as first Director of Educational Services and Student Relations</event>
				</chronitem>
				<chronitem>
					<date>1983</date>
					<event>Special Services Program, Academic Resource Center</event>
				</chronitem>
				<chronitem>
					<date>1983</date>
					<event>Advisor to Minority and Special Students = Sheila Thomas</event>
				</chronitem>
				<chronitem>
					<date>Fall 1990</date>
					<event>Creation of the Office of Multicultural Affairs</event>
				</chronitem>
			</chronlist>
		</bioghist>
		<scopecontent encodinganalog="520">
			<head>Scope and Content Note</head>
			<p>Minutes, reports, correspondence and other material created or collected by the Office of Student Life and Diversity, including records related to the ALANA Center and various student groups. Also included are audiovisual materials, including VHS and compact disc recordings of baccalaureate ceremonies; photographs; event flyers and posters; and realia including mugs, t-shirts, pens, and other give-aways from All College Day, the First Year Experience, and other events.</p>
		</scopecontent>
		<accessrestrict encodinganalog="506">
			<head>Access</head>
			<p>The material in Box 8 is restricted. Certain other files in the collection containing student or personnel information may be restricted pending review by Archives and Special Collections staff. Otherwise, the collection is open for research according to the <extref href="https://library.vassar.edu/specialcollections/policies" show="new"> regulations of the Vassar College Archives and Special Collections Library</extref>without any additional restrictions.</p>
		</accessrestrict>
